{
  "notes": "Lo-fi, E dorian, 90 BPM, almost straight (swing 12: 53 %). A night train: a plucked, guitar-like phase-distortion voice (PHASE RESO PLUCK, the DCW closed a little, a long decay and no sustain, each note ringing into the next) fingerpicking every chord in a rolling dotted-eighth figure, root, fifth, ninth, fifth, tenth, seventh (three against four: the rhythm of the rails), and strumming open chords in A and D; a round sine bass (SUB BASS) on every beat, one and three accented, a fifth below to lead into the bar; the player's Wurlitzer on the Smart Keys (WURLI) over a dorian pentatonic (1 2 b3 5 6: the bright sixth, no avoid notes); and the BOOMBAP kit at a low level, its hats and shaker in a rolling chug. The master is a small carriage: a short sixteenth slapback, a little room, a touch of DUST and ducking. Harmony (no ii or vi, so every ninth in the picking is major): A i7 v7, two bars each; B i7 VIImaj7 IIImaj7 IV7; C IIImaj7 IV7 v7 VIImaj7, climbing and never home (the lift); D IV7 i7, the dorian sigh. At the lowest ENERGY the guitar picks only its eighth-note strings; ENERGY then lets the whole figure through and adds the bass, then kick, snare and eighth hats with the shaker, then the sixteenth chug and fills; it never touches the swing, and the levels give a little back at the top. All material is original.",
